WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540
Look at a cell through
an electron microscope,

2
00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:05.080
and it's packed with odd shapes.

3
00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.900
Each one is an organelle: a
distinct part of the cell,

4
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.800
with a specific job.

5
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:14.140
Membranes inside divide
the cell into compartments,

6
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.980
each with its own enzymes and reactions.

7
00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.810
So how do you tell what each
shape is, and what it does?

8
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.470
In this mission, you'll
open up the nucleus,

9
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.720
which holds the cell's genes and
controls which proteins are made.

10
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:32.840
Then you'll find the mitochondria,
where aerobic respiration makes ATP.

11
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.990
Your mission: work out how to
tell what each shape in a cell is,

12
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.190
and what it does.
